A||||12||johnt671||MSD 6a system what gains ?||||5||
Z||000000||johnt671||07-04-2001||02:48 PM||||Thinking of going to the 6a set up on my 84.  Already have a blaster coil and was wondering what to expect for the bucks. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||07-04-2001||06:30 PM||||I can't give you hp #'s, but I can say that if you're spark plug electrodes are melted, they will still fire with an MSD6aL(same as MSD6a except with rev limiter.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Three of the plugs on my SE V6 has badly damaged electrodes and the car still ran smooth as silk!  That may also be why I stuggled to run 15's at the dragstrip though... <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">     <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||07-04-2001||07:04 PM||||2-3 horsepower depending on the condition of your original ignition system. There are other benefits too like increases gas mileage, smoother running engine, it will never misfire, and lower emissions.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||07-04-2001||07:57 PM||||Sounds good.  It would probably be worth it just to get better gas mileage alone. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||JayUSA77||07-04-2001||09:16 PM||||hey how much are these ignition systems and do they work for all engines including a 94 corvette engine+NoS.<BR>-J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||07-04-2001||09:58 PM||||The MSD's will work in anything and they do make a difference! Makes the pedal very sensitive.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Summit Racing and Jegs sell them at a pretty good price.<BR>Check out either: <A HREF="http://www.jegs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.jegs.com</A> <BR>or: <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000006||Archie||07-04-2001||10:03 PM||||Does anyone have a copy of the MSD installation instructions that they can scan for me? I have 3 used MSD systems but no instructions on hooking them up.<P>TY<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||BV MotorSports||07-04-2001||11:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>Does anyone have a copy of the MSD installation instructions that they can scan for me? I have 3 used MSD systems but no instructions on hooking them up.<P>TY<P>Archie<P>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 07-04-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Archie the easiest way to install a MSD 6 series CD ignition box is to use a GM dual connector wiring harness adapter pn # 8876<BR>(94-95 Camaro/Firebird v8).<BR>Ever notice the v6 Fiero uses the same coil as the early 4th gen F-body?<BR>Plugs in w/o any cutting what so ever. Costs like $20 bucks or so. No more than 5 min to install.<P>Steven<P><P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||14
Z||000008||Tina||07-05-2001||12:36 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Archie:<BR>[B]Does anyone have a copy of the MSD installation instructions that they can scan for me? <P>Sure do.<BR>E-mail me with your fax#,and I'll send it to you. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Tina<BR>BTW Do you want the compatability sheet too.<BR>(ignition and ignition coil compatability)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mach10||07-05-2001||02:49 AM||||I hear that you get a really nifty-looking box! That's a gain, isn't it? <BR>I was always taught that an ignition system won't give you an increase, just recover some loss. However, the stock coil/ICM apparantly starts wheezing at around 4000rpm, while the MSD keeps going. That will give you back a little more upper-end Oomph.||||reg||10
Z||000010||88formula||07-05-2001||09:25 AM||||The net result of recovering a loss is an increase in power right? But you’re right. ||||reg||1
